# The driver roster — the single source of truth for who is in the family.
#
# Every consumer reads this file: scripts/run.sh, scripts/materialize.sh,
# scripts/run-limits.sh, engine/structured/sweep_run.py, oracle/chunk_invariance.py.
# It used to be copied into each of them, which is exactly the shape CLAUDE.md warns
# about — a list kept in five places drifts on the first change that touches four.
#
# Columns, whitespace-separated; `-` means "none":
#
#   name     the driver's name in every report, camp partition and finding write-up
#   builder  the drivers/<builder>/build.sh that produces it
#   arg      the argument that build.sh takes (variant selector), or `-`
#   tags     comma-separated membership tags, or `-`:
#              blocking  runs in the gates that block CI. A driver WITHOUT this tag is
#                        quarantined: still built, still run by a manual or nightly
#                        pass, but kept out of the blocking gates. See below.
#              limits    in the limit-mode roster (scripts/run-limits.sh) — a heap
#                        profile whose corelib can report LIMIT_EXCEEDED
#   binary   path to the built replay driver, relative to the repo root
#
# The four C++ rows are one source (drivers/cpp/driver.cpp) against two corelibs at
# both allow_dynamic settings. The wire format is byte-identical across all four, so
# any divergence between them is a bug by construction — see crucible#129.
#
# The two Kotlin rows are the same shape one level up: one source
# (drivers/kotlin/driver.kt) against one corelib compiled for two Kotlin Multiplatform
# targets — `jvm` (byte-array VarHandles for little-endian word access) and `native`
# (linuxX64 through LLVM, indexed shifts). Same commonMain codec, different machine
# code underneath it, so a divergence between the two rows is likewise a bug by
# construction.
#
# QUARANTINE. A gate selects `blocking` by default; `ROSTER_TAG= ./scripts/run.sh`
# (empty) selects the whole roster, quarantine included, which is how a quarantined
# driver is exercised. The mechanism exists for the same reason
# results/known-clusters.txt does: a gate that is permanently red stops meaning
# "something new broke". A quarantine entry must therefore always name the finding, so
# it can be un-quarantined the moment that finding closes — never a silent exclusion.

# name             builder  arg        tags              binary
c                  c        -          blocking          drivers/c/build/driver
go                 go       -          blocking,limits   drivers/go/build/driver
rust-std           rust     rs         blocking,limits   drivers/rust/build/rs/target/debug/harness
rust-nostd         rust     rs-no-std  blocking          drivers/rust/build/rs-no-std/target/debug/harness
cpp                cpp      cpp        blocking,limits   drivers/cpp/build/cpp/driver
cpp-fixed          cpp      cpp-fixed  blocking          drivers/cpp/build/cpp-fixed/driver
cpp-c-cpp          cpp      c-cpp      blocking          drivers/cpp/build/c-cpp/driver
cpp-c-cpp-dyn      cpp      c-cpp-dyn  blocking          drivers/cpp/build/c-cpp-dyn/driver
py-cython          python   cython     blocking,limits   drivers/python/build/py-cython
py-pure            python   pure       blocking,limits   drivers/python/build/py-pure
java               java     -          blocking,limits   drivers/java/build/driver
typescript         ts       -          blocking,limits   drivers/ts/build/driver
csharp             cs       -          blocking,limits   drivers/cs/build/driver
zig                zig      -          blocking,limits   drivers/zig/build/driver
dart               dart     -          blocking,limits   drivers/dart/build/driver
kotlin-jvm         kotlin   jvm        blocking,limits   drivers/kotlin/build/jvm/driver
kotlin-native      kotlin   native     blocking,limits   drivers/kotlin/build/native/driver
